<<<
artiste. 1. The word is applicable to either sex; artists & artistes as a phrase for male & female performers is a mere blunder.
===
**artiste.** **1.** The word is applicable to either sex; *artists & artistes* as a phrase for male & female performers is a mere blunder.
>>>

<<<
2. In the sense professional singer, dancer, or other public performer, artiste serves a useful p; itis best restricted to this use, in which it conveys no judgement that the performance is in fact artistic;
===
**2.** In the sense *professional singer, dancer, or other public performer*, *artiste* serves a useful purpose; it is best restricted to this use, in which it conveys no judgement that the performance is in fact artistic;
>>>

<<<
if it is desired to intimate that a cook, tailor, hairdresser, &c., or an artiste, makes his occupation into a fine art, artist, & not artiste, is the right word:—He is quite an artist; What an artist!
===
if it is desired to intimate that a cook, tailor, hairdresser, &c., or an artiste, makes his occupation into a fine art, *artist*, & not *artiste*, is the right word:—*He is quite an artist; What an artist!*
>>>

