<<<
as. 1. Equally as. 2. Causal as placed late. 3. As to. 4. As if, as though. 5. As, relative pronoun. 6. Omission of as. 7. As=in the capacity of. 8. Caseafteras. 9. As a jad. 10. As well as. 11. As fo s) &c.
===
**as.** **1.** *Equally as*. **2.** Causal *as* placed late. **3.** *As to*. **4.** *As if, as though*. **5.** *As*, relative pronoun. **6.** Omission of *as*. **7.** *As*=in the capacity of. **8.** Case after *as*. **9.** *As a fact*. **10.** *As well as*. **11.** *As follow(s)* &c.
>>>

<<<
1. For the illiterate equally as (good &c.), see EQUALLY.
===
**1.** For the illiterate *equally as* (good &c.), see ^^EQUALLY^^.
>>>

<<<
2. Causal as placed late, as meaning since, because, seeing that, for, &c. To causal or explanatory asclauses, if they are placed before the main sentence (As he only laughed at my arguments, I gave it up) there is no objection.
===
**2.** Causal *as* placed late, *as* meaning *since, because, seeing that, for*, &c. To causal or explanatory *as*-clauses, if they are placed before the main sentence (*As he only laughed at my arguments, I gave it up*) there is no objection.
>>>

<<<
The reverse order (1 gave it up, as he only laughed at my arguments) is, except when the fact adduced is one _ necessaril known to the hearer or reader present to his mind (J need not translate, as you know German), intolerable to anyone with a literary ear.
===
The reverse order (*I gave it up, as he only laughed at my arguments*) is, except when the fact adduced is one necessarily known to the hearer or reader & present to his mind (*I need not translate, as you know German*), intolerable to anyone with a literary ear.
>>>

